WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.925
Note: This video is part of your Module 1 classroom

00:07.925 --> 00:10.800
instruction. The visit and tour of the mine,

00:10.800 --> 00:13.737
required by Part 48, is a separate,

00:13.737 --> 00:15.100
in-person step.

00:18.412 --> 00:21.125
Welcome to Boonesboro Quarry. This video walks

00:21.125 --> 00:23.662
you through the site before your in-person tour,

00:23.662 --> 00:26.337
so you know where things are and how we work here.

00:26.337 --> 00:29.087
Boonesboro is an underground mine. It produces

00:29.087 --> 00:32.312
crushed stone, from base and DGA to clean stone

00:32.312 --> 00:35.175
sizes. The drawing is an illustration,

00:35.175 --> 00:37.587
not a map. Your instructor will show you the real

00:37.587 --> 00:38.224
one.

00:39.370 --> 00:41.646
The portals are cut right into the highwall.

00:41.646 --> 00:44.408
The sign at the entrance says it's a hard hat area,

00:44.408 --> 00:46.721
so your hard hat and the rest of your PPE go on

00:46.721 --> 00:47.883
before you go in.

00:49.000 --> 00:51.137
Every shift starts at the tag board.

00:51.137 --> 00:53.962
At Boonesboro, the miners' tag board is the covered

00:53.962 --> 00:56.700
board outside. Move your tag to in when you go

00:56.700 --> 00:59.413
underground, and back to out when you come out.

00:59.413 --> 01:02.312
That's how we know who's underground in an emergency.

01:02.312 --> 01:04.875
Never tag in or out for anyone else.

01:04.875 --> 01:07.737
Visitors and contractors check in separately,

01:07.737 --> 01:09.725
on their own board in the breakroom.

01:13.083 --> 01:15.208
Here's how traffic moves on this site.

01:15.208 --> 01:17.721
Haul trucks run between the underground mine and

01:17.721 --> 01:20.546
the plant; road trucks come through the scale.

01:20.546 --> 01:22.883
Pedestrians stay on the marked walkways,

01:22.883 --> 01:25.645
and nobody walks on a haul road. The speed limit

01:25.645 --> 01:29.683
is 15 miles per hour on the surface and 25 underground.

01:29.683 --> 01:32.020
Traffic is two-way and keeps right,

01:32.020 --> 01:33.945
and haul trucks have the right of way.

01:33.945 --> 01:36.520
In a pickup, call the haul truck on the radio before

01:36.520 --> 01:39.395
you approach it. Watch for overhead power lines

01:39.395 --> 01:42.208
on Level 1. Your instructor will show you the actual

01:42.208 --> 01:45.820
haul routes. Remember: make contact with an operator

01:45.820 --> 01:48.221
and get an answer back before you approach any

01:48.221 --> 01:49.133
equipment.

01:50.252 --> 01:53.889
Underground, the travelways run between big pillars.

01:53.889 --> 01:56.790
On 2 West, a caution light marks the intersection

01:56.790 --> 01:59.577
with 5 North. When you see a caution light,

01:59.577 --> 02:02.264
slow down, watch for crossing traffic,

02:02.264 --> 02:03.615
and be ready to stop.

02:04.742 --> 02:07.542
We communicate by radio. On the CB,

02:07.542 --> 02:10.304
the scale house is channel 30 and the yard loaders

02:10.304 --> 02:13.230
are channel 19. Your supervisor will give you any

02:13.230 --> 02:16.267
other channels and the call words. Warning signals

02:16.267 --> 02:19.679
here include the horn and backup alarms on equipment,

02:19.679 --> 02:21.942
the plant start-up horn, and the blast warning

02:21.942 --> 02:22.755
signal.

02:26.100 --> 02:28.863
The basic cycle here is drill, blast,

02:28.863 --> 02:32.688
load, haul and crush. Drilling and blasting are

02:32.688 --> 02:35.800
done by our own Allen crew. Boonesboro is mined

02:35.800 --> 02:38.888
room and pillar, on three levels, and the rooms

02:38.888 --> 02:42.813
here are about 35 by 45 feet. You'll see the mining

02:42.813 --> 02:45.113
method for yourself on your mine tour.

02:45.113 --> 02:47.425
Never work near a highwall or with your back to

02:47.425 --> 02:48.100
one.

02:49.230 --> 02:52.143
The mine shop is underground, on Level 1,

02:52.143 --> 02:55.518
in a big lit opening. Equipment moves in and out

02:55.518 --> 02:58.443
all day, so watch for it, and make eye contact

02:58.443 --> 03:00.630
with an operator before you walk anywhere near

03:00.630 --> 03:01.505
a machine.

03:02.628 --> 03:06.078
Some areas are blocked off, like part of 2 West on the way

03:06.078 --> 03:08.703
toward the Liwell plant and the roll crusher.

03:08.703 --> 03:11.590
A barricade or a warning sign means there's a hazard

03:11.590 --> 03:14.340
you might not see. Never go past one unless you're

03:14.340 --> 03:16.565
authorized and you know the hazard.

03:17.706 --> 03:19.806
The plant is where you'll find crushers,

03:19.806 --> 03:22.881
screens and conveyors; stay on walkways and out

03:22.881 --> 03:25.569
of guarded areas. The shop has its own rules for

03:25.569 --> 03:28.419
lockout and hot work. The scale house is where

03:28.419 --> 03:30.756
trucks are weighed before they leave the pit.

03:34.072 --> 03:36.659
Escapeways are marked on the mine maps with green

03:36.659 --> 03:40.284
arrows. Underground, the primary escapeway is marked

03:40.284 --> 03:43.059
with white reflectors on the ribs, and the secondary

03:43.059 --> 03:46.059
with blue reflectors, along with reflective signs

03:46.059 --> 03:49.509
and arrows. Escape maps are posted in the breakroom

03:49.509 --> 03:52.384
and on each level: in the shop on Level 1,

03:52.384 --> 03:55.184
at the primary crusher MCC on Level 2,

03:55.184 --> 03:58.372
and between the ramps at the porta john on Level 3.

03:58.372 --> 04:01.247
In an emergency, go to a gathering point:

04:01.247 --> 04:03.984
the tag board, or the designated area behind the

04:03.984 --> 04:07.334
mine, outside the 22 North escapeway.

04:08.508 --> 04:11.945
For a serious injury or fire, call 911.

04:11.945 --> 04:15.645
Madison County E911 dispatches all three.

04:15.645 --> 04:20.345
Tell them: Boonesboro Quarry, 2591 Boonesborough Rd,

04:20.345 --> 04:22.858
Richmond, and where the injured person is:

04:22.858 --> 04:26.783
underground, pit, plant, scale or shop.

04:26.783 --> 04:28.995
Then call the mine office so someone meets the

04:28.995 --> 04:32.170
ambulance at the gate. Nearby hospitals are Baptist

04:32.170 --> 04:34.945
Health Richmond, Clark Regional Medical Center,

04:34.945 --> 04:37.933
Baptist Health Lexington ER. Mine rescue comes

04:37.933 --> 04:40.770
from the Kentucky Division of Mine Safety's Crestwood

04:40.770 --> 04:42.958
and Hazard mine rescue stations.

04:44.092 --> 04:46.542
Your in-person mine tour is the next,

04:46.542 --> 04:49.004
separate step. Ask questions about anything you

04:49.004 --> 04:49.742
see.

04:50.854 --> 04:54.016
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

04:54.016 --> 04:55.516
override this video.
